        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Draper Dayton, Wallace L. Dow\n- Places: Worthington, Minnesota, United States\n- Buildings: George D. Dayton House\n- Companies: Dayton's department store, Target Corporation\n- Roles: architect, businessman, philanthropist\n\nFacts:\n- George Draper Dayton was born on March 6, 1857, and died on February 18, 1938.\n- George Draper Dayton was an American businessman and philanthropist.\n- George Draper Dayton founded Dayton's department store, which later became Target Corporation.\n- The George D. Dayton House was built in 1890 in Worthington, Minnesota, United States.\n- George Draper Dayton hired architect Wallace L. Dow of Sioux Falls to design the George D. Dayton House.\n- The George D. Dayton House stood on a parcel that occupied eight lots.",
